      "writtenOn": "2025-09-04T02:41:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What is the high-level approach here? Note in particular we need to support MTLGPUFamilyMac1 which doesn\u0027t support swizzled views.\n\nTwo possible approaches:\n1. The frontend is responsible for composing the requested swizzle with `.r001` if the target is depth/stencil. On Metal Mac1 where that\u0027s not supported, we detect that case and ignore it so the user gets `.rXXX` (X\u003dundefined).\n2. Each backend is responsible for composing the requested swizzle with whatever swizzle it needs (`.r001` in most cases, `.g001` for stencil on D3D, and no swizzle for Metal Mac1).\n\nThere are tradeoffs both ways. Tentatively I think 2 would result in less confusing Dawn code, but I\u0027m not positive. But in this CL, I can\u0027t quite tell what the intended approach is.\n\nI have various comments on the logic but I would need to know what the intent is first.",
      "revId": "8be82ddc2b5bdd40d8f041f76f011bb35f47ba6b",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
